From 98f2a93f104dd8d568efe892328b19327d4363fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:24:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] extcon: sm5502: take the interrupt trigger from the firmware

The driver requests its interrupt as falling edge whatever the firmware
says. With an edge trigger, an event that the chip latches while the
handler is still reading the status registers keeps the line low: there
is no further edge, and no interrupt is seen again until something reads
the status by other means. The vendor driver for the SM5703 MUIC asks
for a low level for this reason.

Leave the trigger to the firmware, so that a board can ask for a level
one. Every in-tree user already describes the interrupt as falling edge,
so nothing changes for them.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
index 6e3d3c7b88..915f39ebaa 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
@@ -833,8 +833,13 @@ static int sm5022_muic_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	/* Support irq domain for SM5502 MUIC device */
-	irq_flags = IRQF_TRIGGER_FALLING | IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED;
+	/*
+	 * Support irq domain for SM5502 MUIC device. The trigger comes from
+	 * the firmware: an event that arrives while the handler is reading
+	 * the status registers keeps the line low, and only a level trigger
+	 * sees it.
+	 */
+	irq_flags = IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED;
 	ret = devm_regmap_add_irq_chip(info->dev, info->regmap, info->irq,
 				       irq_flags, 0, info->type->irq_chip,
 				       &info->irq_data);
